WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.088
Why start here?

2
00:00:01.088 --> 00:00:02.887
The guide opens with one idea.

3
00:00:02.887 --> 00:00:05.763
A Defender license is
not a defended endpoint.

4
00:00:05.763 --> 00:00:08.516
The sensor has to be on
every device and healthy,

5
00:00:08.516 --> 00:00:12.540
the prevention settings have to be
enforced and not just configured,

6
00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:15.788
and every alert has to end in
a decision someone can show.

7
00:00:15.788 --> 00:00:19.374
A license gives you the right to
run the sensor and the service.

8
00:00:19.374 --> 00:00:23.860
It doesn't put the sensor on every device,
it doesn't give anyone the right role,

9
00:00:23.860 --> 00:00:28.488
and it doesn't connect the security
operations center to the tenant's own cloud.

10
00:00:28.488 --> 00:00:32.550
So this module proves three things
before anything else is built.

11
00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.300
The right people can see and act,

12
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:37.800
through roles assigned with
privileged identity management.

13
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:42.925
The S O C reads incidents through
Microsoft Graph, in the tenant's own cloud.

14
00:00:42.925 --> 00:00:46.553
And every in-scope device is
onboarded with an active sensor,

15
00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:49.237
or is in the exception
register with a reason.

16
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:54.120
Gates 1 and 2 come first in the guide,
and every later gate depends on them.
